 ("F7", "Comparative analysis", "PyInstaller 6.22.3, installed into a virtual environment under Python 3.14.6, built python -m PyInstaller --onefile hello.py for a one-line, 23-byte Hello, world program in about 15 seconds, left a build folder, a dist folder and a hello.spec file, and the one executable in dist was 12,950,120 bytes and printed Hello, world!, larger than the chapter's close to 8MB, which describes Windows; python -m pyinstaller in lower case failed with No module named pyinstaller, as the chapter warns, and the PyInstaller manual states that its output is specific to the operating system and the Python version it runs under.", ["P01", "P14"]),
